# Environment for the agent pipeline. Copy to .env and fill in locally.
#
# This file is documentation: it names every variable the skills may read, so a
# new contributor can see the whole surface without reading every skill. It
# carries NAMES and shapes, never values -- `scripts/lint.sh` fails on any
# credential-shaped value in a committed file, and that check is what makes the
# "never commit a secret" rule worth more than a sentence.
#
# .env itself is gitignored. Nothing here is required: every skill runs without
# it, and a missing variable is a named unknown, never a silent default.

# --- Tracker access ---------------------------------------------------------
# The tracker descriptor executes the host's own CLI, which brings its own
# authentication. Set these only when that CLI cannot authenticate by itself.
# GITHUB_TOKEN=
# JIRA_API_TOKEN=
# LINEAR_API_KEY=

# --- Test-environment credentials -------------------------------------------
# Test credentials are always referenced, never inlined: the pipeline config
# holds `credentialsFile` and `passwordEnv`, which NAME the file and the
# variable. The password value never enters the agent's context.
# XEZ_TEST_PASSWORD=

# --- Machine-specific settings ----------------------------------------------
# These belong here, in the environment, and never in
# .xezar/pipeline/config.json -- that file is committed and shared, so a worker
# count or an absolute path in it is wrong on every machine but one. The lint
# gate rejects them there.
# XEZ_MAX_WORKERS=
# XEZ_NODE_MEMORY_MB=
